      "message": "fix(pick): the pick door takes an edge pick whose stitched ring has no area\n\nA plain click on a vertical edge selected nothing, and the first\nCtrl+click on an edge under the first one added nothing: the pocket\nfamily's flat-area door refused the selection, because the stitcher\nwelds open runs whose ends meet seen from above into a ring with no\narea. The door now lets such a stitched collapse in (an edge pick in\nprogress); Generate keeps the refusal and the Geometry page still says\nit. A wall face or a closed chain on a wall is refused as before.\n\nPinned by pick_doors::edge_picks_that_meet_only_from_above_pass_the_pick_door\nand the ui frame tests in egui_app::tests::first_ctrl_click.\n\nFixes #1726\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
